    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ii1ich4",
      "content": "Hindi is written in Devanagari script. The Devanagari script is an abugida :each consonant has an inherent vowel 'a' that is suppressed by adding a halant or by a different vowel matra. Hindi has 52 characters in standard varnamala."
    },
    {
      "id": "gt342ow",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Category</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Characters</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Count</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Swar (Vowels :स्वर)</p>",
            "<p>अ, आ, इ, ई, उ, ऊ, ऋ, ए, ऐ, ओ, औ, अं (anusvar), अः (visarg)</p>",
            "<p>11 main vowels + 2 additional marks</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Vyanjan (Consonants :व्यंजन)</p>",
            "<p>क, ख, ग, घ, ङ (kanthya); च, छ, ज, झ, ञ (talavya); ट, ठ, ड, ढ, ण (murdhanya); त, थ, द, ध, न (dantya); प, फ, ब, भ, म (oshthya); य, र, ल, व (antastha); श, ष, स (ushma); ह (swar-sandhi vyanjan)</p>",
            "<p>33 main consonants + 4 combined forms</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sanyukt Vyanjan (Combined :संयुक्त व्यंजन)</p>",
            "<p>क्ष, त्र, ज्ञ, श्र</p>",
            "<p>4 combined consonants</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Anusvaar and Visarg</p>",
            "<p>अं (bindu/anusvar :nasalisation); अः (visarg :breath sound)</p>",
            "<p>2</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Matra (Vowel Marks)</p>",
            "<p>ा, ि, ी, ु, ू, ृ, े, ै, ो, ौ</p>",
            "<p>10 matras (written forms of vowels when following consonant)</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "r4f9wp9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.2 Shabda Vichar (Word Formation :शब्द विचार)"
    },
    {
      "id": "sks6p57",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Shabda Category</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Sub-type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Examples</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Origin-based Classification</p>",
            "<p>Tatsam (तत्सम)</p>",
            "<p>Directly from Sanskrit without modification; formal register</p>",
            "<p>राजनीति, आकाश, पुस्तक, विद्यालय, कार्यालय</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Origin-based Classification</p>",
            "<p>Tadbhav (तद्भव)</p>",
            "<p>Modified Sanskrit words; changed over time in popular use</p>",
            "<p>हाथ (from हस्त), आग (from अग्नि), घर (from गृह), काम (from कर्म)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Origin-based Classification</p>",
            "<p>Deshaj (देशज)</p>",
            "<p>Words from indigenous non-Sanskrit sources; regional origin</p>",
            "<p>पेट, खिड़की, लड़का, ढोल, जूता</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Origin-based Classification</p>",
            "<p>Videshi (विदेशी)</p>",
            "<p>Foreign loanwords; Arabic, Persian, English, Portuguese origin</p>",
            "<p>किताब, कागज़, कलम (Arabic); बाजार, दुकान (Persian); स्कूल, कॉलेज (English)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Structure-based Classification</p>",
            "<p>Roodhi Shabda (रूढ़ि)</p>",
            "<p>Simple root word; no analysis possible; primary words</p>",
            "<p>पानी, आम, घर</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Structure-based Classification</p>",
            "<p>Yaugik Shabda (यौगिक)</p>",
            "<p>Formed by combining morphemes; analysable into parts</p>",
            "<p>राजभाषा = राज + भाषा; पाठशाला = पाठ + शाला</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Structure-based Classification</p>",
            "<p>Yogrudhi Shabda (योगरूढ़ि)</p>",
            "<p>Compound word but meaning beyond sum of parts; fixed idiom meaning</p>",
            "<p>पंकज (कमल) = पंक + ज; लम्बोदर = गणेश</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "gkb6xyb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.3 Sangya (Noun :संज्ञा)"
    },
    {
      "id": "qv9cvf6",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Hindi</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Examples</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Vyakti Vachhak Sangya</p>",
            "<p>व्यक्तिवाचक संज्ञा</p>",
            "<p>Proper noun; names of specific persons, places, things</p>",
            "<p>राम, गंगा, हिमालय, भारत, दिल्ली</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Jati Vachhak Sangya</p>",
            "<p>जातिवाचक संज्ञा</p>",
            "<p>Common noun; names of class or category</p>",
            "<p>लड़का, शहर, नदी, पहाड़, कर्मचारी</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Bhav Vachhak Sangya</p>",
            "<p>भाववाचक संज्ञा</p>",
            "<p>Abstract noun; names of feelings, qualities, states</p>",
            "<p>प्रेम, सुंदरता, ईमानदारी, आजादी, कठिनाई</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Samuh Vachhak Sangya</p>",
            "<p>समूहवाचक संज्ञा</p>",
            "<p>Collective noun; names of groups or collections</p>",
            "<p>सेना, झुंड, कक्षा, दल, समिति</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Dravya Vachhak Sangya</p>",
            "<p>द्रव्यवाचक संज्ञा</p>",
            "<p>Material noun; names of substances</p>",
            "<p>सोना, चांदी, लोहा, पानी, आटा</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "80xapxf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.4 Sarvanam (Pronoun :सर्वनाम)"
    },
    {
      "id": "noinv3g",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Hindi</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Examples</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Purush Vachhak Sarvanam</p>",
            "<p>पुरुषवाचक सर्वनाम</p>",
            "<p>मैं, तुम, वह, हम, आप, वे (I, you, he/she, we, you-formal, they)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Nishchay Vachhak Sarvanam</p>",
            "<p>निश्चयवाचक सर्वनाम</p>",
            "<p>यह, वह, ये, वे (this, that, these, those)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Anishchay Vachhak Sarvanam</p>",
            "<p>अनिश्चयवाचक सर्वनाम</p>",
            "<p>कोई, कुछ (someone/anyone, something/anything)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sambandh Vachhak Sarvanam</p>",
            "<p>संबंधवाचक सर्वनाम</p>",
            "<p>जो, सो; जो पढ़ेगा, सो पास होगा (who/which/that)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Prashna Vachhak Sarvanam</p>",
            "<p>प्रश्नवाचक सर्वनाम</p>",
            "<p>कौन, क्या, किसे, किसका (who, what, whom, whose)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Nij Vachhak Sarvanam</p>",
            "<p>निजवाचक सर्वनाम</p>",
            "<p>आप :used for oneself; 'मैं आप ही करूंगा'</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bvcigar",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.5 Visheshan (Adjective :विशेषण)"
    },
    {
      "id": "cf0sr4c",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Hindi</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description / Examples</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Gunvachhak</p>",
            "<p>गुणवाचक</p>",
            "<p>Describes quality: अच्छा, बुरा, काला, लाल, लम्बा, ईमानदार, परिश्रमी</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Parimaan Vachhak</p>",
            "<p>परिमाणवाचक</p>",
            "<p>Describes quantity/amount: थोड़ा, बहुत, कम, अधिक, पर्याप्त, सारा</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sankhya Vachhak</p>",
            "<p>संख्यावाचक</p>",
            "<p>Describes number: एक, दो, पहला, दूसरा, कई, कुछ, हर</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sanket Vachhak / Sarvananik</p>",
            "<p>संकेतवाचक</p>",
            "<p>Demonstrative adjective derived from pronouns: यह, वह, ये, वे (as adjective before noun)</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tpmsorg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.6 Kriya (Verb :क्रिया) and Kaal (Tense :काल)"
    },
    {
      "id": "v98dg8k",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Tense Category</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Hindi</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Sub-types</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Examples</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Vartaman Kaal</p>",
            "<p>वर्तमान काल (Present)</p>",
            "<p>Samaanya (Simple), Tatkalik (Continuous), Poorn (Perfect)</p>",
            "<p>वह जाता है / जा रहा है / जा चुका है</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Bhoot Kaal</p>",
            "<p>भूत काल (Past)</p>",
            "<p>Samaanya, Tatkalik, Poorn, Poorntatkalik, Asanna, Sambhavana</p>",
            "<p>वह गया / जा रहा था / जा चुका था / गया था</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Bhavishy Kaal</p>",
            "<p>भविष्यत् काल (Future)</p>",
            "<p>Samaanya (Simple), Sambhavana (Conditional/Probable)</p>",
            "<p>वह जाएगा / जाता होगा / शायद जाए</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "gglppvd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.7 Sandhi (Conjunction of Sounds :संधि)"
    },
    {
      "id": "gmfcb56",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Type of Sandhi</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Hindi</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Rule</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Examples</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Swar Sandhi</p>",
            "<p>स्वर संधि</p>",
            "<p>When two vowels come together; 5 sub-types: Dirgha, Guna, Vriddhi, Yan, Ayadi</p>",
            "<p>विद्या + आलय = विद्यालय; महा + ईश = महेश; सत् + ईव = सदैव</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Vyanjan Sandhi</p>",
            "<p>व्यंजन संधि</p>",
            "<p>When consonant follows vowel or consonant; various rules</p>",
            "<p>जगत् + नाथ = जगन्नाथ; सत् + जन = सज्जन; उत् + लास = उल्लास</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Visarg Sandhi</p>",
            "<p>विसर्ग संधि</p>",
            "<p>When visarg (ः) meets a vowel or consonant; becomes 'r', 'o', 'sh', 's' etc.</p>",
            "<p>मनः + रथ = मनोरथ; निः + छल = निश्छल; दुः + तर = दुस्तर</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ssa7brv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.8 Samas (Compound Words :समास)"
    },
    {
      "id": "wy6l521",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Hindi</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Rule</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Examples</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Avyayibhav Samas</p>",
            "<p>अव्ययीभाव समास</p>",
            "<p>First word is avyaya (indeclinable); whole compound becomes avyaya; usually prepositional</p>",
            "<p>प्रतिदिन (every day), यथाशक्ति (as per ability), आजन्म (for lifetime), निर्भय (fearless)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Tatpurusha Samas</p>",
            "<p>तत्पुरुष समास</p>",
            "<p>Second word dominant; first word shows relationship (in, of, for, from, by); many sub-types</p>",
            "<p>राजपुत्र (king's son), देशभक्त (devoted to nation), पर्वतारोही (mountain climber)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Karmadharaya Samas</p>",
            "<p>कर्मधारय समास</p>",
            "<p>Sub-type of Tatpurusha; one word qualifies other; adjective + noun or metaphor</p>",
            "<p>नीलकमल (blue lotus), महाकवि (great poet), चन्द्रमुख (moon-face)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Dvandva Samas</p>",
            "<p>द्वंद्व समास</p>",
            "<p>Both words equally important; joined by 'and' relationship; reversible</p>",
            "<p>माता-पिता (mother-father), राम-कृष्ण, नर-नारी, आगम-निगम, दिन-रात</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Dvigu Samas</p>",
            "<p>द्विगु समास</p>",
            "<p>First word is numeral; whole compound represents collection or measurement</p>",
            "<p>त्रिलोक (three worlds), सप्ताह (seven days), नवरत्न (nine gems), पंचतंत्र</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Bahuvrihi Samas</p>",
            "<p>बहुव्रीहि समास</p>",
            "<p>Neither word dominant; compound refers to a third entity beyond both; metaphorical</p>",
            "<p>दशानन = दश (ten) + आनन (faces) = Ravana; लम्बोदर = गणेश; नीलकंठ = शिव</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
